¢ AFresh overlying clot (30% chance of rebleed)

While high-risk ulcers require endotherapy, other ulcers (with a clean base) can be treated with medications. Such patients
should be discharged home on medical therapy within 48 hours. There is no need to repeat the endoscopy (option D) for
Liam.

Liam must be started on medications to reduce inflammation and acid secretion. The options include:

e Antacids such as carbonate, Gaviscon
¢ Oral H2-receptor antagonists e.g., cimetidine, famotidine, ranitidine, nizatidine
¢ Regular dose of proton-pump inhibitors (PPI) e.g., omeprazole, lansoprazole, esomeprazole for 4 weeks

PPls at regular doses are commonly preferred medications for the treatment of peptic ulcer disease and are the best option
here. Doubling the dose (option C) while the efficacy of the regular dose is not assessed yet is unlikely to benefit the
patient.

NSAID use and H. pylori infection are the two most common causes of peptic ulcer disease. Biopsy of the stomach and
culture is the gold-standard diagnostic test for H. pylori infection and is performed routinely in patients with peptic ulcer
disease during endoscopy. With a negative biopsy result for H. pylori, other tests for detection of H. pylori infection such as
a urea breath test (option A) or H. pylori serology are (option E) unnecessary.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[40],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-74b2c41bfe2f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"534d4e65df801d683029","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":40,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
