is also often treated with plasma exchange; therefore,\ndifferentiating between HUS and TTP is not as important as in children.\n\nThere is not a single diagnostic test for HUS and TTP. These are diagnosed based on clinical presentation and presence of microangiopathic hemolytic\nanemia presenting with:\n\n1. Anemia, elevated bilirubin, and LDH (often significantly high)\n2. Presence of schistocytes on peripheral smear\n\nIn this case, the presence of micro-angiopathic hemolysis is the most important finding that suggests either HUS or TTP. However, the distinction\nbetween the two is neither possible with certainty nor necessary as the therapeutic approach is almost the same for both HUS and TTP in adults.\n\n(Option A) Thrombocytopenia is almost always a feature of HUS and TTP, as it is in other conditions such as ITP; therefore, it is not diagnostic.\n\n(Option C) Renal function tests, including creatinine, are part of the workup for suspected HUS or TTP but are not diagnostic because high creatinine\nlevels are seen in TTP and HUS as well as dehydration and many other conditions.\n\n(Option D) ADAMTS13 is a metalloproteinase that cleaves Von Willebrand factor (VWF). Its deficiency results in circulating large multimers of VWF.\nLarge molecules of VWF multimers by adhering circulating platelets together lead to microthrombi in the organs, ischemia, and end-organ damage. The\nmajority of patients (>90%) with acquired TTP have circulating antibodies against ADAMTS13 making them ADAMTS13 deficient; however severe\nADAMTS13 deficiency is more common in sporadic forms rather than outbreaks. The test is time-consuming and more prognostic than diagnostic, so it is\nnot routinely ordered. Furthermore, ADAMTS13 deficiency alone does not seem to cause TTP, and a contributing factor such as pregnancy, infection,\ndrugs, etc. is required to trigger TTP.\n\n(Option E) Regardless of the etiology, elevated LDH is seen in hemolysis. LDH is neither sensitive nor specific for HUS/TTP.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","drug","pregnan","therapy"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"36f6ca027ea9fd423350a482856607bb33201f77","duplicate_group_id":"exact-36f6ca027ea9","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a1c04db5801794788e3c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":41,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"85e58dcead10b7405c79","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":2,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"09bcee114297dd903715","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":1,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"48ca170deacae945c19d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":480,"source_qid":"50"}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness