his husband has recently been diagnosed with the disease. Regarding screening for hemochromatosis, which of
the following is the next best in management?',NULL,'D','The gene HFE gene is involved in hereditary hemochromatosis (HH). Mutations in the HFE gene can lead to
impaired regulation of iron storage and clinical manifestations of hemochromatosis. There are two types of
mutation in the ene: C282Y and H63D.

Terminology
¢ Those with only one copy of the mutated HFE (either C282Y or H63D) gene are called heterozygotes.

¢ Those with two copies of the C282Y mutation are called ‘homozygotes.'' Since individuals with two copies of
the H63D mutation never develop clinical hemochromatosis, the homozygote refers to a person with both
copies of HFE with C282Y mutation only.

¢ Those with one copy of the HFE gene with a C282Y mutation and the other with an H63D mutation are
called ‘compound heterozygotes.’ These individuals are often asymptomatic, and if symptoms are present,
they are mild.

About 90% of people of Northern European ancestry with symptoms of HH have the C282Y mutation in both
copies of their HFE gene (homozygote). Two percent are compound heterozygotes (see above).

Since HH follows an autosomal recessive inheritance pattern, there is often no family history, and affected family
members may appear scattered over the generations. If both parents are heterozygous (carriers for a mutation in
the HFE gene), there is a 25% chance that their children will be affected and genetically predisposed to HH.

Current guidelines advise that first-degree and second-degree relatives of individuals who have HH or are
homozygous for the C282Y gene mutation should be tested with iron studies and the HFE gene test. Based on
this recommendation, both children should be considered for testing; however, in this case, testing the mother
would be more convenient and reasonable. If she does not have a faulty HFE gene, no further testing of the
children would be indicated because even if the father is homozygote, the children would only be carriers in the
worst-case scenario.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[45],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0b4789cc9c59","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"cd8cecc4afb255770676","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":45,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"6b5b6211577bd0abfa69","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_page":77,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"755c662fce048d0dee7b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 76-100.pdf","source_page":79,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
