has just been diagnosed with acute cholangitis. Which one of the following statements regarding the
management of acute cholangitis is not correct?','{"A":"Plan for immediate decompression if the patient does not respond to initial measures.","B":"Plan for biliary decompression on a semi-urgent basis (<72 hours) if the patient is responding\nto initial resuscitation.","C":"Plan for urgent decompression (within 24-48hrs) if the patient is older than 70 years.","D":"The most appropriate method of biliary decompression is ERCP, sphincterectomy and stenting.\n\n¥ OE. Initial aggressive resuscitation and antibiotics usually fail to get good response in majority of\ncases.\n\nCorrect\nNo data available now.\n\nExplanation:\nCorrect Answer Is E\n\nAcute ascending cholangitis is initially managed with aggressive fluid resuscitation and intravenous\nantibiotics followed by biliary decompression.\n\nSince the infectious organisms responsible for acute ascending cholangitis are enteric gram-negative\nbacteria, the chosen antibiotic should provide appropriate coverage against these germs.\n\nAll patients with ascending cholangitis require biliary drainage. In about 85-90% of patients, there is a\nresponse to medical therapy. In this group, decompression may be performed semi-electively during the\nsame admission (and ideally within 72 hours)\n\nIn the following patients, urgent decompression may be considered:\n\n¢ Patients older than 70 years","E":"Patients with diabetes\ne Patients with other comorbid conditions\n\nApproximately 10% to 15% of patients (not the majority) fail to respond within 12 to 24 hours or\ndeteriorate after initial medical therapy and need urgent biliary decompression. Delay in doing so\nincreases the chance of adverse outcomes."}','E','Acute ascending cholangitis is initially managed with aggressive fluid resuscitation and intravenous
antibiotics followed by biliary decompression.

Since the infectious organisms responsible for acute ascending cholangitis are enteric gram-negative
bacteria, the chosen antibiotic should provide appropriate coverage against these germs.

All patients with ascending cholangitis require biliary drainage. In about 85-90% of patients, there is a
response to medical therapy. In this group, decompression may be performed semi-electively during the
same admission (and ideally within 72 hours)

In the following patients, urgent decompression may be considered:

¢ Patients older than 70 years
e Patients with diabetes
e Patients with other comorbid conditions

Approximately 10% to 15% of patients (not the majority) fail to respond within 12 to 24 hours or
deteriorate after initial medical therapy and need urgent biliary decompression. Delay in doing so
increases the chance of adverse outcomes.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ded47ccebd1f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5961354bc831a090e0bb","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":63,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"e945f350d5678c08baf3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":107,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"5961354bc831a090e0bb","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":63,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gastroenterology","stem":"You are one of the senior residents in surgery. You are called to see Mr. Kingsley, a 67-year-old man who\nhas just been diagnosed with acute cholangitis. Which one of the following statements regarding the\nmanagement of acute cholangitis is not correct?","options":{"A":"Plan for immediate decompression if the patient does not respond to initial measures.","B":"Plan for biliary decompression on a semi-urgent basis (<72 hours) if the patient is responding\nto initial resuscitation.","C":"Plan for urgent decompression (within 24-48hrs) if the patient is older than 70 years.","D":"The most appropriate method of biliary decompression is ERCP, sphincterectomy and stenting.\n\n¥ OE. Initial aggressive resuscitation and antibiotics usually fail to get good response in majority of\ncases.\n\nCorrect\nNo data available now.\n\nExplanation:\nCorrect Answer Is E\n