has just been diagnosed with acute cholangitis. Which one of the following statements regarding the
management of acute cholangitis is not correct?',NULL,'E','Acute ascending cholangitis is initially managed with aggressive fluid resuscitation and intravenous
antibiotics followed by biliary decompression.

Since the infectious organisms responsible for acute ascending cholangitis are enteric gram-negative
bacteria, the chosen antibiotic should provide appropriate coverage against these germs.

All patients with ascending cholangitis require biliary drainage. In about 85-90% of patients, there is a
response to medical therapy. In this group, decompression may be performed semi-electively during the
same admission (and ideally within 72 hours)

In the following patients, urgent decompression may be considered:

¢ Patients older than 70 years
e Patients with diabetes
e Patients with other comorbid conditions

Approximately 10% to 15% of patients (not the majority) fail to respond within 12 to 24 hours or
deteriorate after initial medical therapy and need urgent biliary decompression. Delay in doing so
increases the chance of adverse outcomes.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ded47ccebd1f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5961354bc831a090e0bb","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":63,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"e945f350d5678c08baf3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 1-40.pdf","source_page":107,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
