 patient has symptoms related to esophageal dysfunction (dysphagia and odynophagia) and established eosinophilia on histological studies. In order for EoE to be the\ndefinite diagnosis, it is necessary that eosinophilia persists after an 8-week trial of a PPI.\n\nThe rationale behind this trial is that GERD may mimic EoE, coexist with it, or contribute to it. Conversely, EoE may contribute to GERD; therefore, the diagnosis of EoE is\ngenerally made after the symptoms persist after an 8-week course of proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) as the best initial step in management. PPIs may benefit patients with\nEoE either by reducing acid production in patients with co-existent GERD or unknown anti-inflammatory mechanisms.\n\nThe main three components of treatment in established EoE are (1) dietary advice and alteration, (2) pharmacotherapy, and (3) surgical intervention. For pharmacological\nintervention topical swallowed steroids (e.g., fluticasone, budesonide) are considered the main treatment options, once the diagnosis of EoE is established either after\nfailed PPI therapy or normal pH studies.\n\nOral (systemic) predniso(lo)ne may be indicated for patients unresponsive to the above measure.\n(Option A) The condition is not infectious and antifungal or antimicrobial agents have no role in treatment.\n\n(Option C) Topical swallowed steroids (e.g., budesonide) are considered as the next step, once the diagnosis of EoE is established either after failed PPI therapy or\nnormal pH studies.\n\n(Option D) Systemic corticosteroids are a treatment option for patients unresponsive to PPIs or swallowed corticosteroids.\n\n(Option E) Eradication of H.pylori has not shown efficacy in the treatment of EoE.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antimicrobial","asthma","guideline","management","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"979761e5e733417ed02c7d6da3bb9dc2ce0f41ff","duplicate_group_id":"exact-979761e5e733","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ed188774115dad3006e4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Git amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":82,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"da5872803c7e3ec9d1a7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 41-75.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 41-75.pdf","source_page":12,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"af30c3e973f1b53a603f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GIT 41-75.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GIT 41-75.pdf","source_page":13,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
